# The changelog blocks whose shape is deliberately what it is, one line per fact.
#
#   scope ~ dimension ~ key ~ reason
#
# Read by .dev/validate/changelog.sh. This is not a suppression list: every line is a claim the run has to
# satisfy. A block with no line here fails the check, and a line here that matched nothing fails it just as
# loudly — the shape it excuses is now correct, so the line has to go. Without that second half the list
# accumulates dead entries and eventually excuses a block that really did open its section twice, which is
# the failure this band exists to prevent.
#
# Wildcards are refused rather than supported. An entry written as a pattern grows silently to cover the
# next block, which is the whole failure it exists to prevent.
#
# A `cross-major` row is refused outright, not merely discouraged. There is no state of the tree in which
# one sentence belongs under two different sections on two majors that ship the same framework, so a row
# excusing one would excuse exactly the defect the dimension was built to catch.
#
# Fields are trimmed, so the columns may be aligned. The reason is mandatory: a line whose reason is empty
# is a line nobody can review.
#
# v3 is not gated — its documents are the next stage's work — and the run reports its findings under a
# count rather than as failures. It therefore has no lines here either.
